invariant: INV-50
file: sha512.c
catches: test/wycheproof.sh
reason: a host object's finalize writes the message's byte count times
  four as the low word of the length where FIPS 180-4 §5.1.2 writes the
  bit count, the byte count times eight. Every digest of a message that
  is not empty is wrong, and every HMAC-SHA-384 and HKDF-SHA-384 output
  with it. The device arm is untouched, so the Wycheproof test that
  compiles a device object passes; the host one runs the HMAC-SHA-384
  and HKDF-SHA-384 suites on sha512.c's first arm under each ch_cfg.cpu
  value it takes, and their first valid case fails.

--- old
// big-endian integer, written into the pending block as the second arm's finalize writes it.
static void finalize(sha512 *s) {
    uint64_t high = s->total_bytes >> 61;
    uint64_t low = s->total_bytes << 3;
--- new
// big-endian integer, written into the pending block as the second arm's finalize writes it.
static void finalize(sha512 *s) {
    uint64_t high = s->total_bytes >> 61;
    uint64_t low = s->total_bytes << 2;
